//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billionaires [link_19]'_Row "Billionaires' Row"). Currently, New York City has 17 supertall buildings, and 2 more under construction. In 2018, two more US cities gained their first supertall buildings: the [Salesforce Tower](link_20) in San Francisco, and the [Comcast Technology Center](link_21) in [Philadelphia](link_22), and in 2025, [Austin](link_23) gained its first ever supertall building, [Waterline](link_24). Construction is ongoing on [Waldorf Astoria Miami](link_25), which would become the first supertall building in [Miami](link_26).

[Mexico](link_27) is the only country besides the United States to have a supertall building in North America – [T.Op Torre 1](link_28) in [Monterrey](link_29), which was built in 2020. [Torre Rise](link_30) is currently under construction in the same city, which would become the tallest building in all of Latin America if completed. While Canada has no completed supertall buildings, it has three under construction – [One Bloor West](link_31), [Skytower at Pinnacle One Yonge](link_32), and [Concord Sky](link_33), all of which are in [Toronto](link_34).

